# Citation File Format 1.2.0 metadata for FailBench.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Qin-z-x/llm-failbench"

cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use FailBench, please cite this repository."
title: FailBench
abstract: >-
  FailBench is an open benchmark and evidence atlas for LLM failure modes. It
  ships deterministic probes across ten failure classes, scored with mechanical
  rules instead of LLM judges, and a curated atlas of publicly reported
  failures. Every atlas record carries a real public source URL; the probe and
  evidence corpora share the same ten-class vocabulary, while per-probe
  evidence ids are reserved for a future release. The kit includes a runner for
  any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, a CI regression gate, and a self-contained
  dashboard. Version 0.1.0 is a
  pre-release: the bundled demo run uses an offline mock provider rather than
  live model calls, and users run the kit on their own endpoint to obtain real
  measurements.
authors:
  - name: "llm-failbench contributors"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation benchmark
  - failure modes
  - hallucination
  - judge-free evaluation
  - determinism
  - regression testing
license: "MIT"
type: software
